      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The conducted study has demonstrated that aged patients with large focal and transmural myocardial infarctions had coagulation changes throughout the acute period of the disease that manifested themselves predominantly in the arterial bed and displayed clear phase-wise fluctuations. The coagulability of peripheral venous blood failed to give a distinct picture of the true state of blood coagulation."},
